Recommends: samba, samba-common-bin, smbclient, cifs-utils
Description: system tweaks for Linux Mint: maintenance, services and Samba
 MintTweaks puts in one GTK 3 window the system chores that otherwise go
 through apt, systemctl, journalctl and smb.conf.
 .
 It covers three areas: disk usage and cleanup (with a preview of what apt
 would remove, and careful removal of old kernels), systemd services with
 their journals and a boot analysis, and complete Samba management with share
 and account administration, testparm validation and automatic backups.
 .
 Privileged actions go through polkit, and every command is run as an argv
 list rather than through a shell.
